reviews.text:
Beautiful hotel but with terrible service… my stay is until June 6th, 2026… If you want to get angry with the service, come to this hotel!

Here is my list of complaints:

1. I asked for a cell phone charger adapter and the concierge promptly said they would bring it to the room. I tried to call again and the phone was never answered. Then I went to reception to ask again and they said they would provide it in 15 minutes, but more than an hour passed and nothing. I went back to beg for the charger and after 30 minutes it was resolved;

2. I went to reception to complain that my key wasn't opening the door and they said that perhaps my room door needed maintenance and that they would arrange for it to be fixed. I returned after 3 hours and nothing was done. I had to go to reception again to say that the door wasn't opening and they said the same thing. I had to wait for the maintenance to be sure they would perform the service;

3. I called the concierge service more than 20 times and they only answered once. I think they should warn that the concierge doesn't answer the phone;

4. I asked three times for the hairdryer to be replaced because the one in my room doesn't work. I still haven't received a replacement;

5. Pay attention to this point… all the cooks handle the food without using gloves, some put their fingers in the ingredients and also in the containers. For us Brazilians, this is very disgusting!

6. It says here that it's an all-inclusive hotel, but if you order a caipirinha with sweetener, they don't say they won't make it because there's no one at the bar to get it. To get my caipirinha with sweetener, I had to go to the bar/café myself and ask them to prepare it so I could take it to the server to make the caipirinha for me.

It's worth noting that this is my list after only 2 days of stay.

My recommendation… the hotel is beautiful but the service is awful, I'll never come back!
